      <processInformation>
        <referenceFunction amount="1.0" category="electricity by fuel" datasetRelatesToProduct="true" generalComment="The average burnup 42.5 MWd/kg heavy metal around year 2000 has been assumed representative for the lifetime of the modeled plant. The average burnup corresponds to an average enrichment of 3.8% U235 for fresh uranium fuel elements. Over the lifetime of the plant it can be assumed that approximately 10% of the energy will be produced by MOX fuel elements. Of total fuel elements 90% are assumed to be from fresh U (thus burdened by the full upstream chain), and 10% MOX (burdened by reprocessing). The utilisation factor for the infrastructure is the inverse of the total net electricity delivered in 40 years lifetime;&#10;UUID: f70df649-dd9e-3fef-b46e-6a867c000041" includedProcesses="The module includes fuel elements, chemicals, and diesel requirements as well as the relevant transport requirements. Water use (fresh and decarbonized) for cooling is included. Considered radioactive waste streams are: spent fuel to reprocessing and conditioning; operational low active waste for conditioning in the intermediate repository; and, contaminated waste from dismantling. Non-radioactive wastes are accounted for." infrastructureProcess="false" localCategory="electricity by fuel" localName="Electricity, nuclear, at power plant pressure water reactor" localSubCategory="waste\nuclear\pwr" name="Electricity, nuclear, at power plant pressure water reactor" subCategory="waste\nuclear\pwr" unit="kWh"/>
